---
interface Props { kind: 'flow' | 'questions'; }
const { kind } = Astro.props;
const questions = [
  {
    name: 'Choice', prompt: 'Which option fits?', question: 'Which story is worth developing next?',
    context: 'Candidate briefs, their source evidence, and the articles already on the blog.',
    answer: 'One of the supplied story options, or “none”, with probabilities for the options.',
    next: 'Use the recommendation to choose what to investigate or draft. The editor still decides the angle.',
    source: 'https://docs.typesafe.ai/primitives/choice',
  },
  {
    name: 'Score', prompt: 'How far along a scale?', question: 'How ready is this story to draft?',
    context: 'The same candidate evidence, plus ordered descriptions: idea only → evidence missing → draftable → concrete example.',
    answer: 'A position along those defined levels, with a distribution over them.',
    next: 'Compare readiness and identify evidence gaps. A relative favorite can still be a weak candidate.',
    source: 'https://docs.typesafe.ai/primitives/score',
  },
  {
    name: 'Noul', prompt: 'Is this supported?', question: 'Does the evidence support this proposed note?',
    context: 'The candidate note and the observations or user statements offered as evidence.',
    answer: 'The probability of “yes”, from 0 to 1. Near 0.5 means uncertainty, not a medium-strength fact.',
    next: 'Combine it with the other capture checks. An agent verifies the evidence before writing a record.',
    source: 'https://docs.typesafe.ai/primitives/noul',
  },
];
---

<figure class="jev-workbench">
  {kind === 'flow' ? <>
    <div class="eyebrow">ONE PATTERN / DIFFERENT JOBS</div>
    <h3>Give the judgment a place in the workflow.</h3>
    <ol class="flow">
      <li><span class="step">01 · TOOLS + CALLER</span><h4>Gather the evidence</h4><p>A note and its sources. A name and search results. A request and known commands.</p></li>
      <li class="model"><span class="step">02 · JEV</span><h4>Ask a focused question</h4><p>Choose an option, assess a defined scale, or judge a yes/no question.</p></li>
      <li><span class="step">03 · CODE + REVIEW</span><h4>Decide what happens</h4><p>Inspect uncertainty, gather more evidence, recommend a next step, or leave the decision open.</p></li>
    </ol>
    <figcaption>Jev receives the context the caller supplies. It does not fetch repository evidence or carry out the next action in these integrations.</figcaption>
  </> : <>
    <div class="eyebrow">THREE QUESTION SHAPES</div>
    <h3>The answer starts with the question.</h3>
    <p class="intro">Open a question type to see how it fits these tools.</p>
    <div class="questions">
      {questions.map((item, i) => <details open={i === 0}>
        <summary><span class="type-name">{item.name}</span><span>{item.prompt}</span></summary>
        <div class="question-body">
          <p class="question">“{item.question}”</p>
          <dl>
            <div><dt>Supply</dt><dd>{item.context}</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Receive</dt><dd>{item.answer}</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Use it</dt><dd>{item.next}</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <a href={item.source}>How {item.name} works <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </div>
      </details>)}
    </div>
    <figcaption>Examples of the questions used by the editorial and knowledge tools, simplified for explanation. This figure makes no API calls and displays no invented model scores.</figcaption>
  </>}
</figure>

<style>
  .jev-workbench { margin: 2.2rem 0; padding: clamp(1.1rem, 4vw, 1.8rem); background: #191527; border: 1px solid #57456e; border-radius: 20px; color: #eee9fa; text-align: left; }
  .eyebrow { color: #c2aaff; font: 600 .67rem/1.5 ui-monospace, monospace; letter-spacing: .12em; }
  h3 { color: #f1edfa; margin: .5rem 0 1.2rem; font-size: clamp(1.2rem, 3vw, 1.65rem); line-height: 1.3; }
  .flow { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: .65rem; list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; }
  .flow li { padding: 1rem .85rem; margin: 0; border: 1px solid #4d3c62; border-radius: 10px; background: #241e32; }
  .flow li::marker { content: ''; }
  .flow .model { border-color: #b79bdc; background: #332345; }
  .step { color: #c6addf; font: 600 .62rem/1.6 ui-monospace, monospace; }
  h4 { color: #f1eaf9; font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.4; margin: .65rem 0; }
  .flow p { color: #d4c9df; font-size: .8rem; line-height: 1.7; margin: 0; }
  .intro { color: #cfc3dd; font-size: .9rem; margin: -.4rem 0 1.2rem; }
  .questions { display: grid; gap: .65rem; }
  details { border: 1px solid #695079; border-radius: 10px; overflow: hidden; }
  summary { cursor: pointer; padding: 1rem; color: #e8ddf8; background: #2c203b; font-size: .9rem; line-height: 1.6; }
  summary:hover { background: #3a294d; }
  summary:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid #79dcc5; outline-offset: -4px; border-radius: 8px; }
  .type-name { color: #d9bafa; font: 600 .95rem ui-monospace, monospace; display: inline-block; min-width: 5rem; margin-right: .5rem; }
  .question-body { padding: 1rem; }
  .question { color: #f0e9fa; font-size: 1rem; margin: 0 0 1rem; line-height: 1.6; }
  dl { margin: 0; }
  dl > div { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 4.4rem 1fr; gap: .6rem; padding: .7rem 0; border-top: 1px solid #44354f; font-size: .83rem; line-height: 1.7; }
  dt { color: #c9ace7; font-weight: 600; }
  dd { color: #d8cce5; margin: 0; }
  .question-body a { display: inline-block; color: #d8b7ff; font-size: .8rem; margin-top: .7rem; }
  figcaption { color: #bdb1cd; font-size: .78rem; line-height: 1.75; margin-top: 1.2rem; text-align: left; }
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .flow { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .flow li { padding: .85rem 1rem; }
    h4 { margin: .35rem 0; }
    summary { padding: .85rem; }
    .type-name { min-width: 4rem; font-size: .85rem; }
    dl > div { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: .1rem; }
  }
</style>
